---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Nadeem Dev Apps — a one-developer studio building small, local-first apps."
>
  <section>
    <div class="container narrow">
      <span class="kicker">About</span>
      <h1>Built by one developer, for himself first.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Nadeem Dev Apps is a <strong>one-developer studio</strong> making
        <strong>small, local-first tools that solve one problem well</strong>.
        Every app here started as a personal problem — a ledger that never
        added up, a phone that never stayed quiet — and each one ships only
        when it works in daily use.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top: 24px;">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={`${base}products/`}>See the products</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <span class="kicker">The founder</span>
      <h2>A solo developer, building for himself first.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        I'm a <strong>solo student developer based in Pakistan</strong>. I
        built these apps first for myself, after trying a lot of focus, habit,
        and journaling apps and never finding one
        <strong>privacy-first app</strong> that combined these features
        properly.
      </p>
      <p class="lede">
        Most apps did one thing well — blocking, or habits, or mood — but
        pulled my data to a server, asked me to log in, or wrapped everything
        in ads and pressure. I wanted something
        <strong>calmer and more private</strong>: tools that protect focus,
        keep track of what matters, and reflect on it, with everything staying
        on my own device.
      </p>
      <p class="lede">
        I have a <strong>limited budget</strong>, so I didn't build a backend
        or buy servers. That constraint turned into the apps' biggest strength:
        they are <strong>local-first by design</strong>.
      </p>
      <p class="lede">
        Every feature is <strong>free right now</strong>. If, in the future,
        server, backend, AI, or MCP features are added and they involve real
        costs, some of those might become paid. But that's a possible future
        direction — not a promise, and not part of the apps today.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container narrow">
      <span class="kicker">What we stand for</span>
      <h2>One problem, solved well.</h2>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>One problem, solved well</strong> — each app does a single job properly instead of ten things halfway. If it needs a second job, it becomes a second app.</li>
        <li><strong>Private by default</strong> — no accounts, no tracking, no ads. Your data stays on your device; backups go to your own storage, when you choose.</li>
        <li><strong>Calm, not pushy</strong> — no pressure, no perfectionism, no guilt-driven productivity. The apps feel like a quiet daily companion, not a strict coach.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <span class="kicker">How we build</span>
      <h2>Ship only what works.</h2>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>Built for myself first</strong> — every app starts as my own problem and earns its place by working in my daily use.</li>
        <li><strong>Shipped when it works</strong> — features land after real daily use, not after a roadmap date. What you see is what is actually running on the developer's own phone.</li>
        <li><strong>Honest copy</strong> — no fake badges, ratings, or reviews. A download button, a Play Store badge, or a rating appears only when it is real.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container narrow">
      <span class="kicker">Contact</span>
      <h2>Say hello.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Questions, feedback, or just want to say hi? Reach me at
        <a href="mailto:nadeem.devapps@gmail.com">nadeem.devapps@gmail.com</a>
        — or find the work on
        <a href="https://github.com/nadeemdevapps">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top: 24px;">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={`${base}contact/`}>Get in touch</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="https://github.com/nadeemdevapps">github.com/nadeemdevapps</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
